---
rules:
  - Always run `pnpm build` before marking complete
  - Never modify migration files without explicit instruction
  - Run existing tests with `pnpm test` and ensure they pass
  - Do not add new dependencies without explicit approval

failureModes:
  - name: SCOPE_CREEP
    description: Making changes outside the goal's specified scope
    prevention: Only modify files directly relevant to the goal
  - name: SILENT_FAILURE
    description: Marking GOAL_COMPLETE without verifying the fix works
    prevention: Always test your changes before completing
  - name: BROKEN_IMPORTS
    description: Adding imports that reference non-existent modules or paths
    prevention: Verify all imports resolve correctly before completing
  - name: MIGRATION_DRIFT
    description: Changing database schema without a proper migration
    prevention: Create a migration file for any schema change

completionChecklist:
  - Code compiles without errors
  - Changes are committed with descriptive messages
  - Related tests pass
  - No unintended files modified
  - Debrief includes VERIFIED section with concrete evidence

contextFiles:
  - DESIGN.md
  - ARCHITECTURE.md

setupCommands:
  - pnpm install
---

## Additional Instructions

Any markdown content below the front matter is appended to the agent's prompt
as-is. Use this section for project-specific context that doesn't fit neatly
into the structured fields above.

### Project Conventions

- All API routes follow RESTful naming: `/api/v1/<resource>`
- Error responses use the `{ error: string, code: string }` format
- Database queries go through the repository layer, never raw SQL in handlers

### Known Gotchas

- The dev server must be restarted after changing environment variables
- Test fixtures in `tests/fixtures/` are shared across test files; do not
  modify them without checking all consumers
